# Local database tooling
.drizzle/

# Claude Code. `launch.json` is committed on purpose — it is what lets the
# preview tooling start the admin dev server, so it belongs to the project
# rather than to one machine. The other two do not: `settings.local.json` is a
# personal permission list, and `worktrees/` holds full checkouts an isolated
# agent run left behind (hundreds of megabytes each). Prune those with
# `git worktree list` and `git worktree remove`, not by deleting the directory —
# they are registered worktrees and one may still hold uncommitted work.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
